      "problem": "Find $|z|$ if $z=2-3\\text{i}.$",
      "worked_solution": "For a complex number $z=a+b\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFor the complex number $z=2-3\\text{i},$ we have $a=2$ and $b=-3.$ So, the magnitude is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}|2-3\\text{i}| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
